# ERP Completion Plan (Strict Frontend-First)

## Summary
Execution is now strictly frontend-first:
1. Build complete UI/routes/forms/flows for all documented screens.
2. Freeze frontend parity against docs.
3. Start backend/API/DB integration in a second pass.

Source of truth:
- `docs/erp_complete_documentation.md.resolved`
- `docs/erp-form-fields-from-screens.md`

## Status Legend
- `✅` Complete
- `🟡` Partial / in progress
- `⬜` Not started

Columns:
- `Route`: page exists and is navigable
- `UI Fields`: documented fields/sections visible in frontend
- `UX Flow`: end-to-end front-end journey wired
- `API/DB`: connected to real persistence (deferred by plan)
- `Tests`: validated with checks/manual scenarios

## KPI Baseline (Updated: February 10, 2026 - Pass 4)
- Route Parity: **100%**
- Field Parity: **73%**
- Flow Parity: **60%**
- API/DB Integration: **38%**
- Test Completion: **28%**

## Phase Order

### Phase 0: Planning Baseline
- [x] Replace old guards-only plan with full 12-module tracker
- [x] Add checklist columns (`Route`, `UI Fields`, `UX Flow`, `API/DB`, `Tests`)
- [x] Add KPI baseline and progress rules

### Phase 1: Frontend Route Parity
- [x] Create missing pages for Payroll, Inventory, Users subpages, Ticketing, Settings, Reports, Imports, Requisitions, Audit
- [x] Fix sidebar targets and broken links (including `/clients/pricing`)
- [x] Ensure every documented screen has a route

### Phase 2: Frontend Form/Screen Parity
- [x] Start documented fields implementation on newly created pages
- [x] Expand Guard Add/Search frontend fields toward UI doc parity
- [x] Expand Client Add/Profile frontend sections toward UI doc parity
- [x] Expand OJT list/new forms with documented filters, action buttons, and table columns
- [ ] Complete field-level parity for all screens

### Phase 3: Frontend Flow and UX Completion
- [x] Improve client search flows (legacy + V2) with real table behavior
- [x] Implement interactive tabbed billing flows for client invoice prerequisites and invoiced billings
- [ ] Complete page-to-page UX flows for all modules
- [ ] Standardize validations/loading/empty/error states
- [ ] Complete responsive behavior pass
- [ ] Freeze frontend after docs parity review

### Phase 4: Backend/API/DB Integration (deferred until frontend freeze)
- [ ] Add/extend Prisma models for missing domains
- [ ] Build missing APIs under module namespaces
- [ ] Replace UI-only placeholders with real persistence
- [ ] Add RBAC + audit logging on mutating operations

### Phase 5: QA, UAT, Hardening
- [ ] Full docs-to-app parity validation
- [ ] Regression + role-based verification
- [ ] Validate reports/imports/requisitions/audit behavior
- [ ] Drive all KPI targets to 100%

